  <section id="beginner">
    <h2>What makes a good beginner river</h2>
    <p>
      Look for a slow, non-tidal stretch with a clear, gentle current, few obstacles and an easy way off the water at either end. Avoid anywhere with weirs without a marked portage, fast narrow sections, low bridges or a lot of overhanging trees. Rivers change with rainfall, so a gentle stretch in summer can be a very different place after a wet week. Read <a href="/blog/river-kayaking-safety-for-beginners/">our beginner safety guide</a> before you go.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="rivers">
    <h2>Rivers to explore</h2>
    <p>
      These rivers are well known for paddling, with plenty of clubs and access points. Always check current conditions and access before you travel.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/rivers/river-thames/">River Thames</a>: long, navigable and busy with boats, with locks and clear portages. Good for gentle touring.</li>
      <li><a href="/rivers/river-wye/">River Wye</a>: a classic multi-day canoeing river between Wales and England, with mainly flat water and occasional easy rapids. Check the current rules for the river's recreational use.</li>
      <li><a href="/rivers/river-dee-wales/">River Dee (Wales)</a>: includes more energetic whitewater sections, and is better for paddlers with some experience or guidance.</li>
      <li><a href="/rivers/river-tweed/">River Tweed</a>: a large Scottish border river with a lot of fishing, so be considerate of anglers.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="planning">
    <h2>Planning your first trip</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Pick a short, easy stretch and check the river level and forecast the day before.</li>
      <li>Confirm launch and exit points and whether you need a licence or permission.</li>
      <li>Paddle with at least one other person, ideally someone experienced.</li>
      <li>Wear a buoyancy aid, dress for the water temperature and carry a phone in a waterproof case.</li>
      <li>Leave your route and expected return time with someone on land.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

